1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:09,601
Your next paper deserves a figure that makes the idea click. Start with three thousand real paper figures, and find the expression that fits your research.

2
00:00:10,401 --> 00:00:22,709
Try RL for reinforcement learning, or world model. Then narrow it down: teaser, mechanism, or experiment. Combine topics, layouts, years, and sources until something clicks.

3
00:00:23,509 --> 00:00:33,625
Already have a draft? Upload your paper, or paste your abstract and methods. Choose the kind of figure you need, and get keyword-based suggestions right in your browser.

4
00:00:34,425 --> 00:00:43,367
Found one you love? Hit Add to project, and choose where it belongs. One reference can live in several projects. Your inspiration stays organized.

5
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:53,084
Open a figure to explore its source, structure, and drawing prompt. Borrow the layout or visual language, then bring your own research to it.

6
00:00:53,884 --> 00:01:03,138
Write what you want to draw. Download the reference pack. Give your drawing agent the images, prompts, and your own method: everything it needs to get started.

7
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:14,340
Agents can search the catalog and manage projects, too. Start with the agent guide. Exchange project JSON with the gallery, and review the selections together.

8
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:22,787
Awesome Academic Figures. Find your next figure. Brief your drawing agent. Open the gallery, and star us on GitHub.
